{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789661309,"nonce":"X/fF6s+o1M3Usd0pHS+YUbLWgNY=","title":"Plumbing CLI: git work issue new|get|list|patch|rm|log with JSON in/out","message":"`git work issue *` is plumbing, primarily agent-driven:\n- JSON output by default; `--format text` for humans.\n- `new` takes a JSON document (arg or stdin) validated against the schema.\n- `patch \u003cid\u003e \u003cjson-patch\u003e` takes RFC 6902 JSON Patch. Chosen over merge-patch because sets (labels, relations) need add/remove, and each patch op maps ~1:1 onto a CRDT op (`replace /fields/status` -\u003e SetField, `add /relations/-` -\u003e AddRelation, `add /comments/-` -\u003e AddComment).\n- `--dry-run` validates and prints the ops that would be committed.\n- `log \u003cid\u003e` prints the op history (the audit trail the weekly report is built from).\nReplaces the bespoke `commands/bug/bug_{title,status,label,comment}*` command tree.","files":null},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789661309,"nonce":"NFf6zSS9ht4S3lN1a7xwXO449YI=","key":"type","value":"task"},{"type":9,"timestamp":1789661309,"nonce":"4UuggBqodK0c4wDmdgLqFSAZYo4=","key":"status","value":"to-do"}]}